# Contract artifacts are hash-verified. Git must not touch their bytes.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows stores LF in the blob while the
# working tree holds CRLF. export_openapi.py then writes a .sha256 sidecar for
# the CRLF bytes, Linux CI checks the file out as LF, and every hash comparison
# fails - a gate that cannot pass on any platform but the one that generated it.
# DMS vendors contract/openapi-1.2.0.json and verifies the same sidecar, so the
# defect crosses the repo boundary.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion, so the bytes are identical in the
# blob, on Windows, and on the CI runner. Frozen specs (1.0.0, 1.1.0) keep the
# exact bytes consumers already vendored.
contract/*.json -text
contract/*.sha256 -text
contract/testvectors/* -text
